  "published": "2026-09-13T10:34:23.51Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.0 — Retargeting release. No public API changes; upgrading needs no caller changes.\n\nBREAKING (target frameworks only):\n- Removed the net6.0 and net7.0 targets; both reached end of life in 2024. Projects still on\n  net6.0 / net7.0 resolve the netstandard2.0 asset instead and keep working, no code changes needed.\n\nADDED:\n- New targets: netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1, net9.0, net10.0. netstandard2.0 extends reach to\n  .NET Framework 4.6.1+ and to any runtime implementing .NET Standard 2.0.\n\nCHANGED:\n- VPageData<T>.PageData and VPageData<T>.PageInfo are initialised to an empty list and an empty\n  PageInfo instead of being left null. Only the parameterless constructor is affected; every other\n  constructor already assigned both. Code that null-checked PageData after using the parameterless\n  constructor now sees an empty page rather than null.\n- Removed the Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub package reference. SourceLink ships in the SDK since\n  .NET 8, so PublishRepositoryUrl + EmbedUntrackedSources give the same result without pulling in\n  the Microsoft.Build.Tasks.Git transitive dependency and its vulnerability advisory. Build-only change.\n\nTECHNICAL:\n- Zero NuGet dependencies on all five target frameworks.\n- First release covered by an automated test suite (MSTest).\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/ozakboy/ozakboy.PageData/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
